<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Anhalt-Plötzkau</h1><p class="st-meta">1603 CE – 1665 CE · capital Plötzkau</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Short-lived Anhalt principality, a minor appanage whose line went on to rule Anhalt-Köthen.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plotzkau">Plötzkau</a>, a small castle district on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saale">Saale</a>, was assigned in the 1603 partition of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-anhalt">Anhalt</a> to August, a younger son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joachim-ernest-prince-of-anhalt">Joachim Ernst</a>. It began as an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> of limited territory rather than a full share, and was formally set up as a principality in 1611.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little distinguishes its government from the other <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-anhalt">Anhalt</a> states: it was a small Calvinist territory administered from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plotzkau">Plötzkau</a> castle, with revenues from farming along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saale">Saale</a>. Its prince August acted as regent for the young princes of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-anhalt-kothen">Anhalt-Köthen</a> and served the joint interests of the Anhalt house during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1665 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kothen">Köthen</a> line died out and Lebrecht and Emanuel of Anhalt-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plotzkau">Plötzkau</a> inherited <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-anhalt-kothen">Anhalt-Köthen</a>, giving up Plötzkau, which returned to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-anhalt-bernburg">Anhalt-Bernburg</a>. The Plötzkau branch thus continued as the ruling house of Köthen until 1847.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/principality-of-anhalt-plotzkau.jpg" alt="Principality of Anhalt-Plötzkau" width="320" height="214"><figcaption>Image: Gedditor · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anhalt-Pl%C3%B6tzkau_map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1603 CE – 1665 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Plötzkau</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>August, Lebrecht, Emanuel</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Calvinism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Anhalt-Plötzkau</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1634&amp;focus=principality-of-anhalt-plotzkau" aria-label="Principality of Anhalt-Plötzkau on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4944 388 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Anhalt-Plötzkau lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5264 644L5276 641M5264 644L5270 644"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5276 641h0M5270 644h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5264 644h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5264 644h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Plötzkau. <a href="/atlas?year=1634&amp;focus=principality-of-anhalt-plotzkau">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
